WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.782
Attention mixes information across token positions, but each token also needs a richer nonlinear

00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:07.832
transformation of its own features.

00:00:07.832 --> 00:00:10.602
That is the job of the feed-forward network.

00:00:10.602 --> 00:00:15.912
A common design takes the hidden vector, projects it to a larger intermediate dimension,

00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:21.687
applies a nonlinear activation such as GELU, and projects it back to the model dimension.

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:27.557
The same feed-forward network parameters are applied independently to every token position in the layer.

00:00:27.557 --> 00:00:34.157
So attention answers, “Which other tokens should contribute information?” while the feed-forward network

00:00:34.157 --> 00:00:38.522
answers, “How should the features inside this updated token vector be transformed?” A residual connection and

00:00:38.522 --> 00:00:42.732
normalization are used here as well.

00:00:42.732 --> 00:00:48.147
Large language models spend a substantial amount of computation in these feed-forward components,

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:51.760
so it is important not to think of the Transformer as attention alone.
